    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Owen Reilly are delighted to present 73 Chancery Street a beautifully refurbished and substantially extended mid-terrace period residence dating from 1913, superbly positioned on this established residential street in the heart of Dublin 7.\r\n\r\nA significant feature of this exceptional home is its substantial two-storey extension, with over 50% of the property's total floor area comprising new-build accommodation. Completed in 2016 under full planning permission, the extension has transformed the property, creating generous contemporary living accommodation while retaining the charm and character of the original period residence.\r\n\r\nThe house has been carefully upgraded and maintained, with original features including cast-iron fireplaces, panelled doors and restored hardwood floors complemented by high-quality modern finishes. Further improvements in 2026 include a newly installed kitchen, new fitted wardrobes and a new front door, ensuring the property is presented in excellent condition throughout.\r\n\r\nOn entering, the generous living room provides a warm and welcoming reception space, with high ceilings, a striking period fireplace and restored hardwood flooring. This leads through to the impressive extended kitchen/breakfast room, with a sliding pocket door providing flexibility between open-plan and more defined living.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen is centred around a large island with granite worktops and benefits from underfloor heating. Extensive glazing and a large Reynaers aluminium sliding door flood the room with natural light while creating a seamless connection with the directly south-facing rear garden. The garden provides a private and attractive setting, with a landscaped patio offering an ideal space for outdoor dining and entertaining.\r\n\r\nA separate utility room and guest WC add valuable practicality to the ground floor.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the first-floor extension has created a generous primary bedroom with two large aluminium double-glazed windows, while the second bedroom is also a well-proportioned double. The accommodation is completed by a spacious family bathroom with bath and quality Villeroy & Boch sanitary ware, along with extensive fitted storage.\r\n\r\nThe property has also benefited from significant investment in its underlying infrastructure, including a complete rewire and replumb, new gas combination boiler, radiators, water tank and water pump. Heating is controlled by a Nest smart system, with additional underfloor heating to the kitchen. Double-glazed acoustic sliding sash windows to the front, internal insulation and other energy-efficiency improvements further enhance comfort.\r\n\r\nCombining substantial new-build accommodation with period character, a superb contemporary kitchen and a rare south-facing garden, 73 Chancery Street offers a turnkey home in an exceptionally convenient Dublin 7 location.\r\n\r\nMore about the location...\r\n\r\nThe location is a particular highlight of 73 Chancery Street, enjoying a prime position in the heart of the city centre. The area offers an exceptional choice of cafés, restaurants, bars, independent shops and cultural amenities, all within easy walking distance.\r\n\r\nThe property is surrounded by some of Dublin’s most notable landmarks and institutions, including the Four Courts, King’s Inns, the Law Library, the Old Jameson Distillery, the Lighthouse Cinema and the National Museum of Ireland at Collins Barracks. Chancery Park and the banks of the River Liffey are also close by, providing valuable green and recreational spaces within the city centre.\r\n\r\nThe TU Dublin Grangegorman campus, Smithfield Village, Phoenix Park, Temple Bar, O’Connell Street and the Jervis Shopping Centre are all readily accessible, while the nearby Red Line LUAS and numerous Dublin Bus routes provide excellent connectivity throughout the city and beyond.\r\n\r\nCombining the convenience of city-centre living with an established residential setting and an area undergoing significant transformation, Chancery Street is exceptionally well positioned to enjoy all that Dublin has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Living Room\r\n(4.54m x 4.23m)\r\nGenerously proportioned reception room with a feature open fireplace and polished floorboards. Open plan to the kitchen/ breakfast room but with sliding pocket doors to provide separation when required.\r\n\r\nKitchen / Breakfast Room\r\n(5.17m x 3.47m)\r\nExcellent range of built in wall and floor units complemented by a polished granite countertop and large island unit with breakfast bar. Integrated appliances to include oven, hob, extractor fan and dishwasher. Tiled floor and large sliding glass patio door to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nUtility\r\n(1.28m x 1.17m)\r\nPlumbed for a washing machine and built in storage,\r\n\r\nGuest WC\r\n(1.4m x 1.38m)\r\nWC, WHB, heated towel rail and tiled floor.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\n\r\nOverlooking the front with a feature cast iron fireplace and built in wardrobes.\r\n\r\n\r\nBathroom\r\n(2.48m x 2.23m)\r\nLarge family bathroom with Villary & Boch sanitary ware to include w wc, whb set in a vanity unit and bath. with overhead shower. Built in storage and heated towel rail.\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\n(3.5m x 3.14m)\r\nLarge double bedroom overlooking the rear garden, with built in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\n\r\nWalled front garden.\r\nThe walled rear south facing garden (6.1m x 4.16m) is set both in patio and lawn."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Large new-build extension with extensive glazing and large sliding doors opening onto the south-facing garden\r\nNewly installed kitchen with large island, granite worktops and underfloor heating, overlooking the garden\r\nDirectly south-facing rear garden with landscaped patio\r\nBright living room with high ceilings, original period fireplace and restored hardwood floorboards\r\nTwo generous double bedrooms, including a large primary bedroom with newly fitted wardrobes\r\nLarge contemporary family bathroom with bath and Villeroy & Boch sanitary ware\r\nSeparate utility room and downstairs WC\r\nFully upgraded, including new wiring, plumbing and gas combi boiler\r\nGas central heating with Nest smart controls\r\nUnderfloor heating to the kitchen\r\nDouble-glazed acoustic sliding sash windows to the front, with internal insulation and double glazing throughout\r\nNew front door, wardrobes and other fittings, all installed this month\r\nResidential on-street permit parking"
